From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt7603: disable RX NAPI before device cleanup

The current netif_napi_del() contract requires a disabled NAPI instance.
MT7603 stops its watchdog through ieee80211_unregister_hw(), but never
disables RX NAPI in successful device removal. Disable registered RX
instances after the final MCU exchange and before shared DMA cleanup.

The watchdog always restores NAPI, and its containing mac_work has been
cancelled by the mac80211 stop callback before this point. Probe failure
does not call this successful-unregister path.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
diff --git a/mt7603/init.c b/mt7603/init.c
--- a/mt7603/init.c
+++ b/mt7603/init.c
@@ -563,9 +563,15 @@
 
 void mt7603_unregister_device(struct mt7603_dev *dev)
 {
+	int i;
+
 	tasklet_disable(&dev->mt76.pre_tbtt_tasklet);
 	mt76_unregister_device(&dev->mt76);
 	mt7603_mcu_exit(dev);
+	for (i = 0; i < __MT_RXQ_MAX; i++) {
+		if (test_bit(i, &dev->mt76.napi_registered))
+			napi_disable(&dev->mt76.napi[i]);
+	}
 	mt7603_dma_cleanup(dev);
 	mt76_free_device(&dev->mt76);
 }
